<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 4 December, from 771 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">771 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,255 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Carloman dies, leaving Charlemagne sole king of the Franks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carloman-i">Carloman I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s brother and co-ruler, died suddenly. Charlemagne took over his kingdom, and Carloman's widow fled with her sons to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carloman-i">Carloman I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Observer is first published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first issue of The Observer appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. It is the world's oldest Sunday newspaper still in publication.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1867">1867 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The National Grange is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Oliver Kelley and colleagues founded the Order of Patrons of Husbandry, known as the Grange, in Washington. It became a powerful voice for farmers against railway rates and monopolies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mary Celeste is found drifting and abandoned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crew of the Dei Gratia found the American brigantine Mary Celeste sailing unmanned in the Atlantic, her cargo intact and lifeboat gone. The fate of the ten people aboard has never been explained.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pan Am ceases operations</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pan American World Airways flew its last flight after 64 years. The airline had pioneered transoceanic air travel and launched the Boeing 747, but it never recovered from deregulation, recession and the Lockerbie bombing.</p></div></li></ol>
